# Slurm job scripts: site-specific (account, partition, QoS) and of no use
# to anyone outside this cluster. Kept locally, never tracked.
*.sbatch
# ...and one that is spelled .sh. An ignore rule cannot match on content,
# so a job script named anything else needs naming here. `git add -A` will
# otherwise re-add it the moment it is untracked, which is what happened.
scripts/slurm_bench_sana_pisa_attention_backend.sh

# MiniMax-H3 GB200 SGLang runtime: a second implementation of the same card,
# kept locally for framework A/B work and not published. Spelled with the
# directory's real case: this rule was written lowercase, and capitalising the
# hardware directories silently stopped it matching, which published the whole
# runtime. tests/ is not published either, but it is still run locally, and
# test_no_private_files_tracked.py fails on any tracked file an ignore rule
# claims -- so a stale rule cannot leak quietly again.
models/minimax_h3/GB200_sglang/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Agent harness. Kept on disk, never published.
#
# What this repository presents is an acceleration pipeline and the methods in
# it -- not the methodology that produced them. These directories are the
# harness: master-agent orchestration, per-node system prompts and decision
# policies for the codex executors, and the goal-session tooling. How the work
# was driven is not part of the deliverable.
#
# They are also dead. 13 of the repository's 16 long-standing test failures
# come from here, and they fail because they shell out to `workflow_lite/`, a
# directory deleted in d2b47a0 and gone from the tree. Nothing on the launch
# path imports any of it: the import closure of scripts/run.py is 21 modules,
# all under scripts/ and techniques/.
workflow/
orchestration/
tools/symposium/
.symposium/
scripts/create_model_experiment.py
tests/test_create_model_experiment.py
tests/test_workflow_lite_topology.py
tests/test_workflow_managed_codex.py

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# One-off probes, audits and benchmarks. Kept on disk, not published.
#
# scripts/ holds three things the launch path needs and thirty that were
# written to answer one question each: probe_public_*_alignment.py comparing a
# local implementation against its published reference, audit_*.py, one-shot
# benchmarks and video-comparison helpers. They are how the methods were
# checked, not the methods.
scripts/*
!scripts/run.py
!scripts/launch_config.py
!scripts/collect_run.py

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tests. Kept on disk and still run locally; not published.
tests/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Development notes. Kept on disk, not published.
#
# docs/ predates site_docs/ by a month and was never folded into it: nothing in
# README.md or on the site ever linked here, so the only way in was to browse
# the file tree. What readers need from it -- the launch interface -- now lives
# in site_docs/installation.md, which is a page the site actually serves. The
# rest is working material: a mechanism-issue log, a workspace contract, an
# onboarding note, and docs/internal/.
docs/
